{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["And Canaan begot — and Put is not written here. And our Rabbis said: [that is,] they supposed that the family of Put was absorbed, until Yeḥezkel came and specified in the passage: ״כוש ופוט ולוד״. And the master R. Yosef Kara asked R. Shmuel: since his family was not absorbed, why did he not write 'and Put begot'? He said: in this passage seventy sons of the sons of Noaḥ are written. From this we learn seventy nations, for it is written in the passage ״מאלה נפרדו״. Now Put and all his sons were only one nation. And had he said 'and Put begot So-and-so and So-and-so,' how could he say ״מאלה נפרדו״, which implies that the nations were scattered from the sons of Noaḥ? [Therefore] he specified each and every one, for if so, there would be more than seventy tongues — therefore he did not write 'and Put begot,' to make known that Put and all his seed were only one tongue."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The bracketed editorial insertions [היינו], [כוש] for [צור], [ו] before פיט, and [ופוט] in the questioner's quotation have been resolved into the running translation. The brief clause אמר) has an unmatched parenthesis in the source; rendered as 'He said' introducing R. Shmuel's reply."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:44:23.460462873Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}